$NetBSD$

Realtek rtw88 (RTL8811CU/RTL8821CU family) chip logic, imported for the
NetBSD USB driver (`rtw88u`, sys/dev/usb/if_rtw88.c).

Origin and licence
------------------

Imported from the out-of-tree lwfinger/rtw88 clone that was verified on
this board by the Linux lane
(doc/rk3568-itx-wiki/runs/20260911-linux-rtl8821au/):

    https://github.com/lwfinger/rtw88.git
    commit a56bcd26e770257612a0803249cbd4095fc6feca (2026-05-21)

Every file below carries "SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause"
and the Realtek copyright notice; they are used here under the
BSD-3-Clause option, exactly as FreeBSD does for the same code
(os/freebsd/src/sys/contrib/dev/rtw88).  The imported files are
unmodified; the NetBSD-side glue lives in ../netbsd/.

Status
------

Import only, staged for the driver port: these files are not yet compiled
into a kernel (no file entries reference them yet).  The closure needed to
drive an 8821CU over USB is:

    main.c main.h util.c util.h tx.c tx.h rx.c rx.h mac.c mac.h
    phy.c phy.h coex.c coex.h efuse.c efuse.h fw.c fw.h ps.c ps.h
    sec.c sec.h bf.c bf.h regd.c regd.h sar.c sar.h
    hci.h reg.h wow.h led.h sdio.h debug.h debug.c
    rtw8821c.c rtw8821c.h rtw8821c_table.c rtw8821c_table.h

Deliberately not imported:

  * mac80211.c, usb.c   - the Linux cfg80211/mac80211 integration and the
                          Linux URB transport; NetBSD gets its own net80211
                          glue and a usbdi(9) transport instead.
  * pci.c, sdio.c       - other buses, not needed for the USB dongle.
  * wow.c, led.c        - optional in Linux (CONFIG_PM / CONFIG_RTW88_LEDS);
                          the header stubs are enough.
  * compiler.h, bitfield.h - Linux-only shims without the dual licence;
                          NetBSD provides its own equivalents.
  * convert_firmware.c  - host-side firmware tool.
